# The Docker build context is the repository root. This file keeps host build output, local state
# and tooling folders out of it; the image restores and publishes from source on its own.

# Host build output. A copied obj/project.assets.json would overwrite the one restored inside the
# container and break the build.
**/bin
**/obj

# Source control, tooling and per-user state
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.vs

# Built indexes and the embedding cache from local runs. The image loads its index at run time.
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose: a **/index pattern could also match the server's
# Index source folder on a case-insensitive file system.
index
index-*
**/.mcpmysite

# Local environment files, which may hold keys
**/*.env
